\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  \cf0   O enter, Lord, Thy temple, be Thou my spirit's guest,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj  Who thro' Thy Spirit gavest a second birth more blest,
\par  Thou in the Godhead, Lord, tho' here to dwell Thou deignest,
\par  For ever equal reignest, art equally adored.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  O enter! Let me know Thee and feel Thy pow'r within;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  The pow'r that breaks our fetters and rescues us from sin.
\par  So wash and cleanse my hearts that I may serve Thee truly,
\par  And render honour duly with perfect heart to Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Thou, Holy Spirit, teaches the soul to pray aright;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Thy songs have sweetest music; Thy pray'rs have wondrous might.
\par  For God doth hear  them all; They pierce the highest heaven,
\par  Till He His help has given who helpeth great and small.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Thou art the oil most holy anointing here Thine own.
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj  This soul, this body lowly, is also Thine alone.
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Thy property are we; as prophets, priests selected,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj  As Kings by Thee elected Thy Holiness  to see.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   Thou art a joyous spirit which sorrow's chains doth break
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Bring comfort thro' Thy merit, our burdens lighter make.
\par  Then Thou so often did with words of love and kindness,
\par \pard        Remove from me the blindness which the joy from me hid.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

